<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Champawat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Champawat is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttarakhand">Uttarakhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumaon">Kumaon</a> hills near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>. Tradition holds that it was the first seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chand-dynasty">Chand dynasty</a> of Kumaon, founded by Som Chand, before the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almora">Almora</a> in the 16th century. It is known for the carved stone <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balasore">Baleshwar</a> temple complex and is the headquarters of Champawat district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/champawat.jpg" alt="Champawat" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WhiteRaven335 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Champawat_town.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
